{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/337150-request-for-splat-book","id":337150,"title":"Request for Splat Book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-12-11T10:00:45-08:00","id":337150,"title":"Request for Splat Book","content":"I would love to see my home in a Splat. A Wraith splat would be very interesting, if not a full multi-game. What city you ask? Kansas City. I'm not going to argue down any other city, or claim KC is more valuable than any other. I know the area some, but would love to see something official.<br /> <br /> Kansas City has been called the City of Philanthropy. Yet the great millionaires of the late 1800's that earned it that title all, or mostly, died peniless. Only one city in the world has more fountains, and that is Rome, hence KC is called the City of Fountains, and uses that symbol on its city flag. The confluence of several rivers (Kaw, Big Blue, Little Blue, and numerous creeks) made the entire region central for travel and trade for Indigenous Peoples. The area was the last place to get fresh water before pioneers struck out on the Santa Caligon Trail (Santa Fe, California, and Oregon). Some very nasty Pre-Civil War and Civil War battles took place in the region; during which the Union behaved such that the locals sided with remnants of the Confederacy for decades after protecting Quantrill's Raiders, the James Gang, and others. Jazz, born in New Orleans, grew up in Kansas City before it settled down in New York. During Prohibition not one ticket was written or prosecution executed for violation of the amendment. Kansas City was popularly known as Paris on the Plains, and during the Pendergast Era (sponsering more than 40 Jazz Clubs at 19th and Vine, a nearby Red-light district, and through public and private works maintained civic development and employment throughout the Great Depression) expanded the city in both size and infrastructure. It is also amusing to not that the very first mafia came from Sicily in the early 1900s (DiGiovani brothers). During the early 1900s Kansas City took part in the Wobbly Free-Speech fights - resulting in many working men being sent to &quot;the Pit&quot; - a prison where reputedly the cots barely hung above the standing water/cesspool in the lowest levels. <br /> <br /> The number of famous people associated with the Kansas City area: <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_people_from_Kansas_City,_Missouri\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>. <br /> <br /> Several interesting resources:<ul><li>Christmastime in Kansas City: The Story of the Season</li> <li>The City of Fountains: Kansas City's Legacy of Beauty and Motion</li> <li>Haunted Kansas City, Missouri</li> <li>Kansas City Chronicles (MO): An Up-to-Date History</li> <li>Kansas City and How It Grew, 1822-2011</li> <li>Kansas City Crime Central: 150 Years of Outlaws, Kidnappers, Mobsters and Their Victims</li> <li>The Mafia and the Machine: The Story of the Kansas City Mob</li> <li>Paris of the Plains: Kansas City from Doughboys to Expressways</li> </ul><br /> At any rate, just a shot for a maybe...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T11:39:37-08:00","id":337263,"title":"","content":"Might as well include the entire state while we're at it. Hwy 13 is a death highway, sadly not the entire road, but the stretch between Humansville and Bolivar. Springfield is almost a Necropolis with all the inner city cemeteries, not to mention Pythian Castle is still an active haunt. Republic has Wilson's Creek Battlefield, another active haunt. Not to mention with so many cemeteries at random locations, they would be outposts in the Shadowlands.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T13:40:45-08:00","id":337377,"title":"","content":"My longest running Wraith game was set in KC. I did A LOT of research to get the history in play and a lot of creative thinking to get the Necropolis proper set up. I really enjoyed it. As did the players. <br /> <br /> My second longest running Wraith game was set in St. Louis...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:19:19-08:00","id":337570,"title":"","content":"The term Splat is usually used to describe things like Clans, Tribes and Traditions, organizations to which your character belongs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:23:53-08:00","id":337575,"title":"","content":"Another American setting? No thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-11T17:50:37-08:00","id":337592,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the cWoD is americanocentric enough as it is. How about a Wraith suplement for Scandinavia? I'd love to see some Norwegian wraiths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4449-eisenkreutzer","name":"EisenKreutzer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4449_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T03:14:39-08:00","id":337907,"title":"","content":"I'm actually wokring on Necropolis Stockholm for my own amusement, so I'm all for Scandinavia! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4427-malfean_sleepover","name":"Malfean_Sleepover","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4427_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T12:45:18-08:00","id":338275,"title":"","content":"The book has to SELL to be worthwhile. <br /> <br /> I don't think KC has the cachet of New York City, Boston, New Orleans, LA, etc., etc. So, no matter how cool it is, who is going to buy it? <br /> <br /> Same goes for expecting things from most non-USA countries. You have to get an audience interested. Which means it's got to a be well known place that's interesting enough to attract buyers with things with being interesting in both a Wraith and non-wraithly sense who know enough about it to not be put off by unfamiliarity factors like different country, different language. And that's to the majority of Wraith players. Who probably aren't Scandinavian or well-versed in things Scandinavian, don't know anything especially cool as detailed in Wraith so far about Scandinavian places, etc.<br /> <br /> A great non-US site to see would be Florence. Since it's canon that it's majorly effed up. Or London, since it's the first &quot;official&quot; Necropolis. Or Rome... because... ya know.... Stygia and all. <br /> <br /> Oddly, for the US, Detroit seems like it would be ripe for a Wraith setting book. LOTS of Relic buildings and such coming through. I can see Necropolis Detroit being a center of industry of sorts. Building comes through, break it down for spare parts and ship them off on rails.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T13:05:51-08:00","id":338289,"title":"","content":"If I had more money than I could possibly handle I would shower it at Onyx to release a New Zealand book just for inevitable comparison between Geist and Wraith.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T14:46:34-08:00","id":338449,"title":"","content":"Detroit Necropolis?? I like it, especially if you add a bit on Windsor too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Interestingly enough I think Montreal (Canada) could make for a good Necropolis too (in addition to be a Sabbat City). Istanbul and Paris too would make great Necropolis book,...especially Paris France whose catacombs are world famous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.catacombes.paris.fr/en/homepage-catacombs-official-website\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://www.catacombes.paris.fr/themes/custom/catacombes_theme/dist/images/logo-catacombes.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.catacombes.paris.fr/en/homepage-catacombs-official-website\" target=\"_blank\"> The Paris Catacombs | Catacombes de Paris | Official website </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.catacombes.paris.fr/en/homepage-catacombs-official-website\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.catacombes.paris.fr/en/homepage-catacombs-official-website </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Project consolidation:<br /> Rough Draft: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1230422-rough-idea-for-a-werewolf-mini-supplement\" target=\"_blank\">Dhole Shifters</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1212511-city-book-seeking-advice\" target=\"_blank\">Ottawa By Night</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1194394-fanon-tribebook-bunyip-wip\" target=\"_blank\">Tribebook Bunyip</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/353881-your-new-revamped-tribes?p=354143#post354143\" target=\"_blank\">Garou Variant</a><br /> In redaction: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1151956-%E1%B9%A3ill%C4%81nu-b%C4%93lu-lasombra-bloodline-feedback-request\" target=\"_blank\">Lasombra Bloodline</a>","edited":{"userid":3226,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","user":"Boneguard","date":". 12-12-2014, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3226-boneguard","name":"Boneguard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3226_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T15:59:37-08:00","id":338525,"title":"","content":"Istanbul would make a mind-blowing Necropolis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-12T17:19:40-08:00","id":338572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/337150-request-for-splat-book?p=338525#post338525\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Istanbul would make a mind-blowing Necropolis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would LOVE this. <br /> <br /> With one reservation. I can't remember Constantinople By Night all that well... but I would hope that any continuity with Dark Ages precedents would not undermine the unbelievable coolness of Necropolis Istanbul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T11:55:26-08:00","id":339255,"title":"","content":"Three cities in one, pretty much, rare are cities that exemplify fading glory like Bizantium.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:07:45-08:00","id":339269,"title":"","content":"I gotta agree on Paris being extremely interesting city for a Necropoli book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1629-possessed","name":"Possessed","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1629_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1140"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T12:55:22-08:00","id":339352,"title":"","content":"Same Above as Below plotline?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1442-paladindemo","name":"PaladinDemo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1442_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"622"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T13:30:22-08:00","id":339401,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see a Necropolis London or Paris book. Any of the old European cities would be great fodder for a Necropolis book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T18:42:26-08:00","id":339634,"title":"","content":"A humble suggestion of mine would be to feature Warsaw. WW2 is a sensitive topic to handle, but with enough care it can be tackled. The essence of Warsaw is that nominally it's centuries old capital, but it's at the same time one of youngest capitals since it indeed 'died' in 1944, the city except for Praga district razed down, the civilians dead or displaced, rural population flocking to the city seeking new prospects when the communist authorities decided to rebuild it. Contrast the now-dead Paris of the North (as people referred to Warsaw pre-1939) with the modern city with new identity forged from ashes. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:08:45-08:00","id":339653,"title":"","content":"Maybe but there partially is in <i>Charnel House</i>s <i>of Europe</i>. One of the places they explore is the Warsaw Ghetto, one of the Necropoli of the Dark Kingdom of Wire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T19:35:56-08:00","id":339691,"title":"","content":"Fresh start demands fresh expansion books, as we are in mid 2010s now. Lots of things changed, and besides Warsaw is not only about Ghetto Uprising:<br /> <br /> - Warsaw Uprising of 1944 makes look said Uprising minor in scope<br /> <br /> - There is more history to Warsaw than WW2. 1650s and 1790s Warsaw witnessed and suffered a lot, for example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cI am absolute, I am perfect, I am supreme. I shall be eternal. My tragedy, is that there is no other fate for me. My powerlessness was that I couldn\u2019t subjugate my journey to the gods, while dreaming of rebirth at the end of distant time, like other pharaohs.\u201d Ramesses II, Fate/Prototype: Argent Fragments.","edited":{"userid":2918,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","user":"Kat","date":". 12-13-2014, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2918-kat","name":"Kat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2918_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1762"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-13T23:53:36-08:00","id":339780,"title":"","content":"My interest in Kansas City is partially in how well it fits into all the campaigns. It is a limited population metropolis with a current metro-population of around 2.4 million in over a dozen counties (7,952 sq. mi./20,596 sq. km). It has a history that involves multicultural aspects from several indigenous peoples (both native to the area and relocated from further east). There are strong immigrant traditions from the English, French, Germans, Hungarians, Irish, Italians, Jews, Mexicans, Scots, etc. The Asian Chamber of Commerce in KC includes members who are Chinese, East Indian, Filipino, Japanese, Korean, and Vietnamese. There is an international airport in the sparsely populated north, and another airport downtown. The one would be great for Werewolf movers and shakers, while the other is perfect for Kindred to arrive further inside the city - away from the dangers of the wild. The setting contains some interesting religions - remnants of the Spiritualists movements of the late 1800s, a few Mormon splinter groups, Amish and Church of the Brethren, Judaism, Islam, Sikhs, Bahai, and Unity Village which has a strong ancient Egyptian symbolism in its structures. Famous African American heritage tie ins include Negro Leagues Baseball and the development of Jazz as a cultural influences. It's sister city is Seville Spain, and there could easily be a Lasombra Anti-tribu connection in not only that choice - but the architecture of KC's most prominent and exclusive business district is designed from that of its sister city. The area is full of potential as not merely a book for wraith, but for cross game and cross cultural influences.<br /> <br /> Now, as to why ST supplements may be more American centered has much to do with the knowledge base of those who created the game. It is difficult, especially in a nation where political correctness marches to the drums it confiscated from the Gestapo, to create said materials. If those materials are in any way <i>'perceivable'</i> as stereotypical then the company will be trounced for carrying to the stereotype. If the product does not have the role models (stereotypes) that players want to role play then they will be equally disappointed and feel the culture they like is slighted. Thus far, the World of Darkness has done a relatively fantastic job of navigating those waters - but not without complaints by those who choose to be offended by the minor imperfections in their efforts. (Instead of choosing to be exalted with the brave efforts to do the best they can with the resources available to them.)<br /> <br /> If they were to do a region of the world, for <i>a game</i>, about which they can only know what is printed for them to read - then the result would be limited to what American English readers can conceive in the translated reports of such materials. Should they even employ experts in that region, then the results will either be from Academics whose materials will defensible from a legal standpoint or from native non-academics whose results will carry local limitations (read bias) as well as insights to which academics cannot ascribe (unverifiable oral traditions about events - myth). (For instance here in the KC area there still exist oral stories of the barbarity of Union oppression during the Civil War. Accusations of murder to steal property rights for the Union affiliated banks, elite, and train companies, theft of property by Jay Hawkers, slaughtering of livestock and burning of crops, placement of women and children in concentration camp like conditions after the brutal murders of all males 11 years of age and up, etc. The academic history and the oral myth differ but are both based on real events. The best way for supplements from so far afield to be developed in my mind, would be from the direct offerings of those native to those regions, and familiar with the game mechanics and existing lore, to develop and donate them - accepting whatever editing Onyx Path may provide, and then allow them to be published. A precedent for this exists in video games like Neverwinter Nights where the player community was able to create longstanding additional materials (mods and haks) for the game which were then published through the Bioware website supporting the game.<br /> <br /> And to re-emphasize what I said before, I am not down-playing any other city or region. I was just asking for Kansas City - a city whose corrupt political machine put the man in the White House who won WW II and then had that same political machine dismembered by morally justified reformers whose politics have left it gutted in prominence, tarnished in glory, and bereft of interest in the national spotlight. What better place for secret and monstrous societies to run rampant than the hidden heart of the country?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cIt was clear to me for a long time that the origins of science had their deep roots in a particular myth, that of invariance.&quot; ~ Giorgio de Santillana<br /> Preface to Hamlet's Mill","edited":{"userid":2345,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","user":"Whithers","date":". 12-14-2014, 03:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2345-whithers","name":"Whithers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:16:04-08:00","id":340112,"title":"","content":"This is not super original, but I would love a setting book detailing New Orleans (and if they threw in Baton Rouge and Shreveport for measure I would jizz my pants).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T10:30:14-08:00","id":340120,"title":"","content":"Might as well take all the suggestions and make a Necropoli Across the World book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters I back.<br /> W20, MtC, CB20, DtD, MtAs20, BotW20, Wraith 20th.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","da