ue":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"477"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T15:20:38-08:00","id":340251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/337150-request-for-splat-book?p=339255#post339255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Three cities in one, pretty much, rare are cities that exemplify fading glory like Bizantium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Byzantium may be long gone and Constantinople may be a name of the past, but there is nothing &quot;fading&quot; about Istanbul. I have never been to a city more poised and confident and full of delicious, lovely Pathos about where it will be in the future. The layering and juxtaposition of those along with what shadows you'd see cast in the cramped and winding alleys of Istanbul in the World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Gorgeous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T23:31:06-08:00","id":340557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Boneguard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.th